    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T01:10:34Z",
    "body": "cause: the march's ground (finishing3d::support::support_at) answered only strict facet tangency, so between two facets with sky normals m1, m2 the annulus r*|m1-m2| (0.47 mm between the hill's 9-degree bands at r 3) had no answer at all - the ball genuinely rests on the shared edge there. Rows broke at every fold and the ridge scan read the hole as cusp. Decision taken: add the drop-cutter edge contact (ball against segment, the edge arm of the vertex/facet/edge decomposition) for CONVEX folds between shallow facets; concave folds, mesh rims and shallow-steep edges stay strict. Every candidate still passes the exact ball_clear.",
