    "created_at": "2026-11-07T01:24:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T01:24:04Z",
    "body": "staged (uncommitted) in worktree agent-a5fd58ff693cf5698: new finishing3d/edge.rs adds the drop-cutter edge contact for convex folds between shallow facets. It is admitted only when the contact normal lies on the arc m1->m2 and only after it passes the exact ball_clear. The arc test also keeps knife rims (like a cap's base disc) out. Release readings against the 0.123 gate: hill contour/radial/spiral (with and without ramp) went from 0.126-0.144 to 0, ramp hill from 0.154 to 0, dome multidirection from 0.125 to 0. The ratchet table is down to one entry: tilted ramp at 0.170. That reading is unchanged because the shelf is one plane with no fold, and the hop path reads the same 0.1698 at the high rim corner (7.19, -7.81), so it has a different cause and needs its own issue. finish3d_radial_dome.cl re-blessed: 1736 -> 1874 moves, plunges 246 -> 150. Debug finish3d/flow, the release --ignored lane, app golden_cl and operations all pass, and clippy is clean.",
